# Forge's route search orders the quests of this guide and its guide writer writes the steps.
# Fixes go into data/route-fixes.json, data/guide-fixes.json or forever-db/corrections, never
# into this file.
# Added here: To the Undercity for Yagyin's Digest (728), News for Fizzle (1137).

# The Badlands at 39-40, the last zone of Horde 30-40 (the 2026-11-07 re-order; they followed
# Arathi at 37-38 before, and the route went back to Stranglethorn, Orgrimmar and Dustwallow
# from Kargath).
#
# Flow: Faldir's Cove (where the previous guide ends) -> the Thandol Span, the Wetlands and
# Loch Modan -> the Valley of Fangs (Martek, Rigglefuzz) -> Lotwil's camp -> Kargath (flight
# path) -> the lesser rock elementals -> Lotwil -> the slabs by Agmond's End -> Agmond's End ->
# the Stonevault troggs -> the Valley of Fangs -> the Uldaman dig -> Agmond's End -> the coyotes
# and Giant Buzzards of the basin -> Lotwil -> Kargath, from where the next guide flies to Grom'gol.
#
# The basin's Giant Buzzards (39-41) and Elder Crag Coyotes (38-40) come last, on the way back west
# to Lotwil and Kargath (0.4.3 round): after the slabs, the troggs and Rigglefuzz's wings, players
# below 40 finish the gizzards and coyote drops near the Valley of Fangs and Hammertoe's Digsite instead.
#
# The slabs come from the Rock Elementals beside Agmond's End, and Lotwil takes them on the way
# back to Kargath (2026-11-09 audit): no walk back to his camp from the basin in between. Left
# out: his third study (712, bracers from the level 42-44 Greater Rock Elementals) and Lucien's
# Stone Is Better than Cloth after it (716, crafted bracers).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Into the Badlands

step Into the Badlands
  zone Badlands
  tip Head for the Thandol Span, the great bridge at Arathi's southern edge, cross it and follow the road south through the Wetlands to the Dun Algaz tunnel into Loch Modan. Thelsamar, the dwarf town on the road in the middle of Loch Modan, has guards who attack the Horde: leave the road before it and pass the town on the hills to its west. The road leaves Loch Modan to the south into the Badlands; follow it to the goblin camp in the Valley of Fangs.
  goto 42.3,52.8 "Valley of Fangs"

step Valley of Fangs
  turnin 1106                         -- Martek the Exiled: Fizzle's letter from the Shimmering Flats
  accept 1108
  accept 703                          -- Rigglefuzz

step The Dustbowl
  tip Head west along the road towards Kargath; Lotwil's camp sits in the Dustbowl halfway there.
  accept 710                          -- Lotwil Veriatus

step Kargath
  tip Kargath is the Horde fortress built into the cliffs at the zone's western edge. Neeka Bloodscar stands on Kargath's upper level, high above the flight master: take the ramps up, the arrow cannot tell the levels apart.
  getfp "Kargath"
  accept 1419                         -- Neeka Bloodscar
  accept 1420                         -- for Helgrum in Stonard, around level 42
  accept 2258                         -- Jarkal Mossmeld, inside
  vendor nearest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Around the Dustbowl

step Lesser Rock Elementals
  tip The small elementals drift across the flats between Kargath and Lotwil's camp, on the road back east. Every rock elemental in the zone can drop Jarkal's Rock Elemental Shards.
  collect 4626 quest 710
  collect 7848 npc 2735 quest 2258.3 @13.1,39.2 map 1418

step Lotwil Veriatus
  turnin 710
  accept 711

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The south
step Rock Elementals
  zone Badlands
  tip South-east from Lotwil's camp across the basin, the bigger Rock Elementals (39-40) stand on the slopes west of Agmond's End; each one drops a slab. At 38, take the level 39s. Every rock elemental can drop Jarkal's Rock Elemental Shards. The Feral Crag Coyotes (37-38) on these hills drop Neeka's jawbones and Jarkal's fangs too: take them as you meet them. Careful: Malevolent Mirages (42, elite) drift across these slopes too.
  loop
  goto 40.4,75.8 map 1418
  goto 41.8,77.1 map 1418
  collect 4627 npc 92 quest 711
  collect 7848 npc 92 quest 2258.3

step Agmond's End
  when group 709
  tip Theldurin sits among the dwarven ruins at Agmond's End, just east of the elementals. His tablet lies just inside Uldaman's cave mouth, beside level 38 elites: a quest for a group.
  accept 709

step Stonevault troggs
  tip The Stonevault troggs dig around the cave mouths south of the Valley of Fangs, on the way north from Agmond's End; the Bonesnappers and Shamans drop the flakes. The Buzzards for Rigglefuzz's wings circle the hills between the Valley of Fangs and Agmond's End. Hunt Stonevault Bonesnappers (39-40) for the flakes. At 38, pick the 39s; leave the Shamans (40-41) alone.
  collect 5797 npc 2893 quest 1108 @50.2,67.1 map 1418

step Buzzards by the Stonevault hills
  zone Badlands
  tip Gather Rigglefuzz's wings from the Buzzards on these hills. Leave the giants to the west alone.
  loop
  goto 49.5,63.8 map 1418
  goto 50.3,60.0 map 1418
  collect 3404 npc 2830 quest 703

step Feral Crag Coyotes
  when level<40
  zone Badlands
  tip On the hills beside the Buzzards, the Feral Crag Coyotes (37-38) drop both jawbones and fangs. Leave the Giant Buzzards of the western basin for higher levels.
  loop
  goto 52.4,60.6 map 1418
  goto 56.7,61.0 map 1418
  collect 6166 npc 2728 quest 1419
  collect 7846 npc 2728 quest 2258.2


step Valley of Fangs
  tip The road north to Uldaman runs through the Valley of Fangs: Rigglefuzz and Martek take the wings and the flakes on the way.
  turnin 703                          -- Rigglefuzz
  turnin 1108                         -- Martek the Exiled
  accept 1137                         -- for Fizzle at the Mirage Raceway, on the way from Freewind Post to Tanaris around level 43

step Ancient Chest
  when group 709
  tip Keep north on the road to Uldaman's entrance, in the north of the Badlands: the chest lies just inside the cave mouth. Magregan Deepshadow and the Obsidian Golems (38) stand beside it and Shadowforge Diggers (35-36) work the tunnel, all elite: keep your group together.
  collect 4631 quest 709              -- Below ground

step Starving Buzzards
  when level<40
  zone Badlands
  tip Still short of gizzards after gathering Rigglefuzz's wings? Hunt the Starving Buzzards (35-37) north of Hammertoe's Digsite. They drop gizzards more often than the Buzzards at the Stonevault hills. Stay away from the roaming Malevolent Mirages (42, elite).
  loop
  goto 57.5,28.6 map 1418
  goto 58.8,24.3 map 1418
  collect 7847 npc 2829 quest 2258.1

step Agmond's End
  when group 709
  tip Head back south down the road, past the Valley of Fangs.
  turnin 709                          -- Theldurin the Lost
  accept 728

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The basin, on the way back west
step Badlands: kill these as you meet them
  when level>=40
  zone Badlands
  tip West from the Valley of Fangs towards Lotwil's camp, the Elder Crag Coyotes and Giant Buzzards roam the basin south of the Dustbowl. Coyotes drop both the jawbones and the fangs; the Giant Buzzards drop the gizzards. Careful: Malevolent Mirages (42, elite) drift across the Badlands: give them a wide berth.
  tip Pull the Giant Buzzards (39-41) one at a time. The Ridge Stalker Patriarchs (40-41) prowl the same slopes towards Kargath: leave them. The Buzzards (37) you killed for Rigglefuzz's wings drop gizzards too, more rarely.
  loop
  goto 33.4,59.8 map 1418
  goto 25.8,61.9 map 1418
  collect 6166 npc 2729 quest 1419
  collect 7846 npc 2729 quest 2258.2
  collect 7847 npc 2831 quest 2258.1

step The Dustbowl
  tip North-west across the basin to Lotwil's camp. Short of Jarkal's shards? The Lesser Rock Elementals (37-39) on the flats west of the camp drop them about one kill in five.
  turnin 711                          -- Lotwil Veriatus
  note Lotwil's next study wants bracers from the Greater Rock Elementals (42-44) in the south-western gulches, well above you: leave it.
  collect 7848 npc 2735 quest 2258.3 @19.1,45.8 map 1418

step Kargath
  tip Head west back to Kargath. Neeka Bloodscar stands on Kargath's upper level, high above the flight master: take the ramps up, the arrow cannot tell the levels apart. The Riverglades, Forever's new zone, lie south of the Badlands through the pass of Twilight's Shroud; the route goes there at about 41, after Stranglethorn Vale and the Swamp of Sorrows. Careful if you go now: the Twilight camps of Da'grosh's valley, right below the pass, are 43-46, with Twilight Enforcers (45, elite) on patrol and Overlord Kilgar and Executioner Morg (46, elite) in the fortress. Going anyway? Load the Riverglades guide: it starts at Rog'mar, east along the valley, away from those camps.
  turnin 1419                         -- Neeka Bloodscar
  turnin 2258                         -- Jarkal Mossmeld, inside
  note The next guide flies from Kargath to Grom'gol.
